<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan Telecom up 1.55 percent.</title>
<headline>Pakistan Telecom up 1.55 percent.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan Telecommunication Company Ltd (PTCL) shares jumped 0.55 rupees, or 1.89 percent, to 29.60 on Friday after the government announced it was cutting excise duty and seeking a reduction in inter-city call charges, dealers said.</p>
<p>Finance Minister Sartaj Aziz, in his budget speech for fiscal 1997/98 (July-June), slashed excise duty on telephone calls to 25 percent from 40 percent and said the government would urge PTCL to reduce inter-city call charges by 20 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;It is a good announcement, but it was expected,&quot; dealer Sajjad Mankani said. -- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
